The plate looks like a dinner plate, about 26 cm across. Each of the three meatballs measures roughly 3.5 to 4 cm across, so about 4 cm. That gives a volume of about 33 cm³ each, and at a density near 0.9 that is roughly 25 to 30 g per ball. The three together come to about 80 g.

Sausage-style balls like these run about 250 kcal per 100 g, so 80 g is about 200 kcal. The balls look baked, possibly sausage and cheese, and I can't see any visible oil or sauce.

